= Conclusion

The integrated pipeline at its binary defaults reaches mean mask IoU $0.748$ and mean boundary $F_1$ $0.194$ across a $55$-frame hand-labeled subset spanning eleven distinct VARTM infusion runs, well above the two reimplemented prior classical-CV pipelines on every region metric (Lekanidis-Vosniakos 2020: IoU $0.144$; Almazán-Lázaro 2022: IoU $0.075$). The headline number is bounded by the temporal-locking startup-transient that the per-sample ablation surfaces. A per-sample component-removal ablation on the same subset reports the marginal IoU effect of disabling each named primitive in turn; the marginal effects vary by sample, and the per-sample breakdown rather than the eleven-sample mean is the load-bearing piece. From that breakdown, a regime-indexed configuration lookup translates the per-sample evidence into preprocessing settings indexed by the run circumstances a practitioner can read off their own bench. The empirical contribution of this paper is the integrated pipeline as a named composition, the per-sample evidence that names which components do the work on which infusion regimes, and the lookup that translates that evidence into preprocessing settings for the next infusion that lands on the bench.
